{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:2abc4f528cb7d6ca","name":"R-1 Recon Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-2abc4f528cb7d6ca","title":"R-1 Recon Droid","revision":19549,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:10:27Z","sha256":"95113bd863039b5f4fbeaa54ad685edcae063d80fbb8ec120b5afbbb6df83eb6","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19549","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=R-1%20Recon%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-2abc4f528cb7d6ca","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Although ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}," doesn't trust ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," to serve as combatants, it does employ Military Droids in combat roles as scouts and forward observers. One the earliest of these is the R-1, built by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Arakyd Industries"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Arakyd_Industries","referenceId":"reference:53475569f2ae9d67"}," and based on designs originally developed by ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"},". A small floating Droid, the R-1 lacks tools or hands, but it can move through openings that most of its potential targets can't. Combined with its integral blaster, this allows the R-1 to track most prey with ease, and occasionally even take out a foe itself.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The R-1 is popular with snipers, planetary garrisons, and shock troops. It has a limited broadcast range (a single planet), but can be used to scout areas without risking a living observer, spot targets for long-range sniper fire or orbital bombardment, seek out wanted criminals, or follow suspects back to a base of operations. Though the Empire officially does not sanction sales of the R-1 to anyone else, many do find their way into the hands of bounty hunters and other independent operators.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["R-1 Recon Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["R-1 Recon Droid Statistics (CL 1)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n","Small ",{"tag":"a","children":["4th-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/4th-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scout"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scout","referenceId":"reference:8a1db462be753774"}," 1\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +8; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +9\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic (understand only), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},", 1 Unassigned\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 16 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fl